.TH BRINE 1 "2026-10-23" "brine" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
brine \- run Roblox Studio on Linux under Wine, with MCP support
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B brine
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B brine
installs, updates and runs Roblox Studio under Wine directly on the host, as
the invoking user, without Flatpak or any other sandbox. Studio's built-in MCP
server is exposed to Linux MCP clients such as Claude Code and Claude Desktop
through
.BR "brine mcp" .
.PP
brine never needs root and refuses to run as root. It is not affiliated with
Roblox Corporation.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup \fR[\fB\-\-runtime\fR \fIauto|system|managed|PATH\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
First-run wizard: choose a Wine runtime, create the prefix, install Studio,
WebView2 and DXVK, and install desktop entries and URI handlers. Safe to run
again to repair an installation.
.TP
.B install \fR[\fB\-\-force\fR]
Install the current Studio build.
.TP
.B update
Install a newer Studio build, keeping the previous one.
.TP
.B rollback
Switch back to the previous Studio build and pause automatic updates until the
next explicit
.B install
or
.BR update .
.TP
.B run \fR[\fIFILE\fR|\fIURI\fR|\fIADDRESS\fR] [\fB\-v\fR]
Start Studio. A
.I .rbxl
or
.I .rbxlx
file is opened as a place;
.I roblox-studio:
and
.I roblox-studio-auth:
URIs are passed to Studio (this is how browser sign-in completes).
A roblox.com/games/<id> or create.roblox.com/dashboard/creations/experiences/<id> address is turned into an
"Edit in Studio" link. Only plain Roblox links are accepted; anything that could add arguments to Studio's
command line is refused. When started without a terminal (by a browser or file manager) with a link or file,
brine returns immediately and Studio runs in the background.
.B \-v
copies Wine's output to the terminal.
.TP
.B kill
Stop Studio and the prefix's wineserver.
.TP
.B mcp
Run the stdio MCP server that MCP clients launch. See
.BR "MCP INTEGRATION" .
.TP
.B mcp connect claude\-code \fR[\fB\-\-scope\fR \fIuser|local|project\fR]
Register brine with Claude Code (\fBclaude mcp add\fR).
.TP
.B mcp connect claude\-desktop
Merge brine into \fI~/.config/Claude/claude_desktop_config.json\fR, keeping a
backup and every other server. Invalid JSON is never overwritten.
.TP
.B mcp disconnect claude\-code|claude\-desktop
Undo the above.
.TP
.B mcp enable
Turn on Studio's "Enable Studio as MCP server" setting while Studio is closed.
.TP
.B mcp test \fR[\fB\-\-luau\fR \fICODE\fR] [\fB\-\-wait\fR \fIDURATION\fR]
Round-trip
.B list_roblox_studios
and optionally
.BR execute_luau .
.TP
.B mcp \-\-print\-config
Print configuration for manual client setup.
.TP
.B doctor \fR[\fB\-\-quick\fR]
Check Wine, Vulkan, the prefix, Studio, WebView2, desktop integration, the MCP
setting and a full MCP round trip, and print a fix for each problem.
.TP
.B runtime update
Download or update the managed Wine build.
.TP
.B desktop install|remove
Install or remove the desktop entry, MIME types, icon and URI handlers.
.TP
.B winecfg, regedit, wine \fIPROGRAM\fR
Run Wine tools inside brine's prefix.
.TP
.B config
Show the configuration file location and effective settings.
.TP
.B uninstall \fR[\fB\-\-purge\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR]
Remove desktop integration and MCP registrations. With
.B \-\-purge
also delete the Wine prefix (which holds the Studio sign-in), Studio builds,
configuration, logs and caches. The brine program itself is left for the
package manager.
.TP
.B completion bash|zsh|fish
Print a shell completion script.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH MCP INTEGRATION
Studio ships a helper, StudioMCP.exe, that listens on 127.0.0.1:13469 and
that Studio connects to. \fBbrine mcp\fR runs it from the active Studio build
inside brine's prefix, with the same Wine binary, wineserver and environment
as Studio. It speaks newline-delimited JSON-RPC on stdin/stdout; only valid
JSON-RPC is ever written to stdout, and everything else goes to the log. When
Studio is not running, tool calls fail immediately with a clear message
(unless \fBautostart_studio\fR is set). The helper is restarted if it dies,
and \fBbrine mcp\fR exits when its standard input closes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/brine/config.toml
Configuration (TOML). Sections: [wine], [graphics], [studio], [mcp], [env], [fflags].
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/brine/
prefix/, versions/, runtimes/, state.json.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/brine/
studio.log, mcp.log, brine.log. Credentials and auth codes are redacted.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/brine/
Downloads.
.PP
The XDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME and XDG_CACHE_HOME variables
are honoured.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Brine sets WINEPREFIX, WINEDEBUG, WINESERVER and WINEDLLOVERRIDES for the
processes it starts and ignores any values inherited from the caller.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on failure, 2 on a usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wine (1),
.BR claude (1)
